Data licensing for FAR
======================

This project publishes three kinds of data and they are NOT under one licence.
Read this before redistributing any of it.

1. WHAT THIS PROJECT CREATED  ->  CC0 1.0 Universal (public domain)
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   The curated mapping tables and everything derived from them:

     data/platforms.json      data/natives.json       data/links.json
     data/namespace-gaps.json
     the CAIP-19 identifiers this project constructs
     the family classification, the accuracy measurements, the prose

   https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

2. DTIF REGISTRY CONTENT  ->  NOT ours to license, and NOT CC0
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   DTI codes, DLI codes, long names, short names, ISINs, group structure,
   anchor block hashes, distributed-ledger references and technical
   references originate in the ISO 24165 registry operated by the Digital
   Token Identifier Foundation.

   DTIF's terms state: "We and/or our licensors are the owner(s) of all
   intellectual property rights in our Site and the Materials. Nothing in
   these Terms operates to transfer ownership of any intellectual property
   rights."

   This project therefore CANNOT and does not place that content in the
   public domain. It appears in:

     data/sources/dti-registry.json.gz        data/sources/dtif-*-full.json.gz
     data/ledgers.json      data/dti-identities.json
     dist/dti/*.json        dist/ledger/*.json         dist/far.json[.gz]
     the search index, and any route carrying a DTI or DLI

   DTIF grants redistribution on two conditions, which bind you as they bind
   us: you must not modify the Registry in any way which could be misleading
   to any person, and you must not charge any person for any redistribution
   of the Registry. See SOURCES.md for the full wording and for how this
   project obtained the data.

3. OTHER UPSTREAM SOURCES  ->  their own terms
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   CoinGecko ids and contract mappings, ethereum-lists/chains (MIT),
   SLIP-0044 (MIT). See SOURCES.md.

A NOTE ON WHY THIS FILE IS THIS LONG. An earlier version said the published
dump was CC0 without qualification. That was wrong: it purported to dedicate
DTIF's registry content to the public domain, which this project has no right
to do and which would have misled anyone relying on it.
